# Production Checklist: {{ .Group.Name }}

This checklist turns the generated API scaffold into a business-ready skill.

## Product / Business

- [ ] `SKILL.md` description names real user intents, synonyms, and boundaries.
- [ ] Core concepts explain business entities, IDs, URLs, states, ownership, and permissions.
- [ ] `command-routing.md` covers common user phrases and commands to avoid.
- [ ] `workflows.md` covers the top 3-5 business tasks.
- [ ] Cross-skill routing is documented for out-of-scope requests.
- [ ] User-facing output expectations are documented: fields, URLs, status, and next steps.

## Engineering

- [ ] `{{ .App.Name }} {{ .Group.Name }} --help` works.
{{- range .Group.Operations }}
- [ ] `{{ $.App.Name }} {{ $.Group.Name }} {{ .CommandName }} --help` works.
{{- end }}
- [ ] Required parameters, body fields, and header rules in `SKILL.md` match the CLI.
- [ ] Complex JSON input documents `--data` / `--file` shape clearly.
- [ ] Authentication, environment variables, and base URL setup are accurate.

## Safety

- [ ] Write, delete, bulk, clear, reset, import, and irreversible operations require confirmation or a documented exception.
- [ ] Missing IDs are resolved through list/search/get, not guessed.
- [ ] Ambiguous search results require user selection.
- [ ] Workflows include read-back verification where the API supports it.
- [ ] Permission and tenant boundaries are documented.

## QA

- [ ] Front matter is valid and the skill loads.
- [ ] Every documented command exists.
- [ ] At least one read-only example runs successfully.
- [ ] At least one write workflow is dry-run tested or tested in a safe environment.
- [ ] Empty result, invalid parameter, not found, and permission denied paths have recovery guidance.
- [ ] Known limitations are listed before handoff.

## Maintenance

- [ ] API or MCP schema changes trigger regeneration and review.
- [ ] CLI command renames update `SKILL.md` and `references/`.
- [ ] Business rule changes update workflow and routing docs.
- [ ] Verification evidence is recorded in the PR or release notes.
